      text: "The Bargain of Rumpelstiltskin: A foolish miller boasted to the king that his beautiful daughter could spin ordinary straw into pure shining gold. Intrigued by such miraculous wealth, the greedy monarch locked the terrified girl inside a tower room filled to the ceiling with bundles of straw, threatening her with execution if the task was not completed by dawn. As the girl wept bitterly in the darkness, a strange little man appeared from the shadows, offering to spin the straw into gold in exchange for her precious necklace.\n\nThe next morning, the king was overjoyed to find the room filled with glittering gold, but his greed was insatiable. He locked the girl in an even larger room filled with straw. Once again, the mysterious small man appeared, spinning all the straw into thread in exchange for her ring. On the third night, when the girl had nothing left to give, the small man demanded a terrible price: her firstborn child once she became queen. Desperate to save her life, the miller daughter agreed to the tragic bargain.",
