      id: "2m-5",
      text: "The Little Mermaid Sacrifice: Deep below the sea, the youngest mermaid princess possessed a voice sweeter than any creature in the ocean realm. Yet she would trade all her aquatic beauty for a human soul and two legs to walk on land beside the prince she had saved from a shipwreck. Desperate to join the human world, she swam down to the dark abyss where the sea witch resided amidst writhing tentacles and glowing sea creatures.\n\nThe sea witch agreed to craft a potion that would transform her fish tail into human legs, but warned that every step on land would feel like walking on sharp knives. Furthermore, as payment for the potion, the witch demanded the princess golden singing voice, cutting out her tongue before handing over the vial. If the prince married another maiden, the little mermaid would dissolve into sea foam on the morning after his wedding, losing her immortality forever.",
